# Based on github/gitignore's Go template, plus this project's own artifacts.

# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool, specifically when used with LiteIDE
*.out

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# ---- project-specific ----

# `go build` output. Go names the binary after the module, so on Unix it has no
# extension and none of the patterns above match it.
/hallway

# Conference data, fetched from the public Sessionize API at runtime. Not
# committed: it changes daily, and both binaries download it on demand — the
# server automatically, `cmd/report` with -refresh.
/all.json
/speakers.json
*-all.json
*-speakers.json

# Embedding cache: large, provider-specific, and rebuilt on demand.
*.embeddings.json

# Generated reports. cmd/report always names its output
# <event>-<company>-YYYY-MM-DD.md, so match that date suffix rather than all
# markdown — otherwise docs like CONTRIBUTING.md get ignored by surprise.
*-[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9].md
